<http://data.silknow.org/event/4237b0ab-f952-37c8-b34b-87caef12adb2>
        a                              ecrm:E8_Acquisition ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Gift of N. & C. Six Mejonkvrouwe, Jachtlust, Netherlands. Given along with T.718-1972 another silk and T.717-1972 a worsted (RP 72/2705). The note in the registered papers indicates that the Six family 'are an old and distinguished Dutch family and the father of the donors did the standard work on linene damasks many years ago'. The Rijksmuseum has duplicates of these three pieces and put the donors in touch with the V&A."@en ;
        ecrm:P14_carried_out_by        <http://data.silknow.org/actor/4a8e4b2f-5df1-3654-b123-28f0e3c6928f> ;
        ecrm:P22_transferred_title_to  <http://data.silknow.org/actor/f0577f91-f887-3019-bf88-f9e5ba019390> ;
        ecrm:P23_transferred_title_from
                "Given by Mejonkvrouwe N. Six and Mejonkvrouwe C. Six" ;
        ecrm:P24_transferred_title_of  <http://data.silknow.org/object/2c223987-9892-31d7-a991-6cb75fb39214> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "Gift of N. & C. Six Mejonkvrouwe, Jachtlust, Netherlands. Given along with T.718-1972 another silk and T.717-1972 a worsted (RP 72/2705). The note in the registered papers indicates that the Six family 'are an old and distinguished Dutch family and the father of the donors did the standard work on linene damasks many years ago'. The Rijksmuseum has duplicates of these three pieces and put the donors in touch with the V&A."@en .

